<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Daehan Flour seeks 21,200T U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Daehan Flour seeks 21,200T U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daehan Flour Mills Co Ltd has invited tenders to buy 21,200 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat by 2:00 p.m. (0500 GMT) on Friday, traders said.  </p>
<p>Traders said the 21,200 tonnes of U.S. wheat would be split into three lots -- 6,300 tonnes of western white/soft white, 3,500 tonnes of hard red winter (protein minimum 11.5 percent), and 11,400 tonnes of dark northern spring (protein minimum 14 percent).</p>
<p>Shipment was set for August 5-September 5 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>--Seoul newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
